annotations.description:
{{ if $values.A }}The root APFS volume on macOS runner host {{ $labels.instance }} ({{ $labels.env }}) has under 10% free for 15m (currently {{ $values.A.Value | printf "%.1f" }}%).{{ else }}No root-filesystem percentage is available. Check the query, exporter targets and ingestion before treating this as healthy capacity.{{ end }}

Tart golden images and runner cache volumes share the host disk. tart-kubelet reclaims goldens at 15% free and reports DiskPressure below 10%; this alert is the backstop if reclaim cannot keep up, for example when every golden backs a live clone.

Compare root filesystem metrics with exporter up and the runner Node inventory. For low space, follow the runbook to inspect host disk use and golden/cache retention. For missing data, verify both rented and rack host coverage; never map missing telemetry to healthy free space.
